{
  "//": [
    "Environment separation lives here. Three named aliases, three distinct Firebase",
    "projects, selected with `firebase use <alias>` or `--project <alias>`.",
    "",
    "`dev` points at a `demo-` project id, which the Firebase emulator suite treats as",
    "an offline project: nothing in this repo can reach a real backend by accident.",
    "`staging` and `prod` are intentionally placeholders in this reference repo — see",
    "README > 'This repo never deploys'. Replace them in a real fork.",
    "",
    "The hosting targets keep the end-user app and the admin console on separate sites",
    "so they can be deployed, rolled back and access-controlled independently."
  ],
  "projects": {
    "default": "demo-reference-flutter-firebase",
    "dev": "demo-reference-flutter-firebase",
    "staging": "REPLACE-WITH-STAGING-PROJECT-ID",
    "prod": "REPLACE-WITH-PRODUCTION-PROJECT-ID"
  },
  "targets": {
    "demo-reference-flutter-firebase": {
      "hosting": {
        "app": ["demo-reference-flutter-firebase"],
        "admin": ["demo-reference-flutter-firebase-admin"]
      }
    }
  }
}
